    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0313" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d162-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 452/25</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-08">8 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">British Participation in the War
                        Against Japan</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Reference: C.C.S. 452/18<anchor n="2" xml:id="d162-f2"/></p>
                <p>The United States Chiefs of Staff accept the British proposal in C.C.S. 452/18
                    for the formation of a British Empire task force under a British commander,
                    consisting of British, Australian, and New Zealand land, sea and air forces to
                    operate in the Southwest Pacific Theater under General MacArthur’s supreme
                    command. It is noted that this will enable the British Fleet to be well placed
                    to reenforce the U.S. Pacific Fleet if this should later be desired.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d162-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d162-f1-content">
                <p>For the discussion of the subject of this paper by the Combined Chiefs of Staff
                    at their 174th Meeting, September 14, 1944, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg331">p. 331</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d162-f2" n="2" xml:id="d162-f2-content">
